+--------+
|Confettysh|
+--------+

Confettysh runs an SSH server that plays terminal visual effects for
connecting clients.  It is a public, unauthenticated demonstration
service: anyone who can reach the port can connect and view the
effects.  Do not run it on an untrusted network without a packet
filter rule.

The rc.d(8) script runs the server as the _confettysh user with
/var/db/confettysh as the working directory.  Host keys are written to
/var/db/confettysh/.ssh and persist across restarts.

	doas rcctl enable confettysh
	doas rcctl start confettysh

By default the server listens on 0.0.0.0:2222 and also exposes the
Prometheus metrics endpoint on 0.0.0.0:9222.  Both addresses come from
the single -listen flag.  Override the defaults in /etc/rc.conf.local,
for example:

	confettysh_flags="-listen 127.0.0.1 -port 2222 -metrics-port 9222"

Connect with:

	ssh -p 2222 localhost
